        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dcda8ef6-553e-51ab-aa2a-578d6ed294c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dawn French, Jennifer Saunders, Al Pillay, Lana Pellay, Adrian Edmondson, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, Robbie Coltrane, Gary Clail\n- Works: The Supergrass, French and Saunders, The Vicar of Dibley, Eat the Rich, The Comic Strip Presents, Gino, Human Nature, Emotional Hooligan\n- Roles: actress, writer, comedian, backing vocalist\n\nFacts:\n- Dawn Roma French was born on 11 October 1957 and is an English actress, writer, and comedian.\n- Al Pillay was born on 22 August 1959 and is also known as Al Pillay.\n- Dawn French is best known for starring in and writing for the comedy sketch show French and Saunders with Jennifer Saunders.\n- Dawn French also played the lead role of Geraldine Granger in the sitcom The Vicar of Dibley.\n- Al Pillay starred in Eat the Rich.\n- In The Comic Strip Presents, Al Pillay appeared as Alan Pellay playing Himself in the episode Gino.\n- In The Comic Strip Presents, Al Pillay also appeared as Alana Pellay playing Herself in episode 13.\n- In the feature film The Supergrass, Al Pillay appeared as Lana Pellay playing Mary.\n- The film The Supergrass starred Richardson, Adrian Edmondson, Jennifer Saunders, Dawn French, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, and Robbie Coltrane.\n- The song Human Nature by Gary Clail On-U Sound System features Lana Pellay on backing vocals and appears on the album Emotional Hooligan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
